                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Basic Information[/h1]\n[b]Title:[/b]  Color Chaos\n[b]Developer:[/b]  Daniel Riley\n[b]Publisher:[/b]  Daniel Riley\t\n[b]Genre:[/b]  Casual\n\n[h1]General Impression[/h1]\nColor Chaos is a seemingly simple yet thoroughly fun, little 3D casual shooter. Its objective is equally straightforward: obtain and always strive to increase your high score by obliterating as many enemies as possible. The difficulty is well scaled and by going from Classic to Chaos Mode, you can substantially increase the challenge while the Turbo modes, up the ante even further. The presence of Achievements, Cards and even a Leaderboard, make this small competitive title, a good break from the complexity of other games. The beautiful neon glows and chromatic diversity are sadly not complemented by a worthwhile soundtrack. Being part of the twin-stick shooter subgenre, means that Color Chaos is obviously best played on a controller, but I had little difficulty enjoying it on the traditional mouse & keyboard layout. While I noticed that some buyers have complained, I do not think that this game is overpriced given the overall state and functionality in which Color Chaos is to be found right now. Dubstep music aside, I had a lot of fun with it and I do hope it shall receive further support in the future.\n \n[h1]Strong Points[/h1]\n+ Good looking and stable gameplay.\n+ Several game modes to choose from.\n+ Steam Trading Cards & Achievements.\n\n[h1]Weak Points[/h1]\n- Limited sound selection.\n\n[b]Rating 7/10[/b]\n \n[quote]This review was submitted for [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/ImperialReviews]Imperial Reviews[/url] and [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/Cubbes]Cubbes[/url].[/quote]",
